WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:09.095
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:14.891
Unit ten: Question Tags (basic). Today you will check information with question tags.

4
00:00:15.191 --> 00:00:17.913
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:22.065
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:24.011
Isn't it?.

7
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:29.538
Isn't it? means a question tag after a positive sentence with is.

8
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.662
It is hot, isn't it?

9
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.461
Your turn. Say: Isn't it?.

10
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.197
Isn't it?.

11
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:39.777
Don't you?.

12
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:45.375
Don't you? means a question tag after a positive present simple sentence.

13
00:00:45.983 --> 00:00:47.611
You like tea, don't you?

14
00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:50.579
Your turn. Say: Don't you?.

15
00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:54.202
Don't you?.

16
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.079
Question tag.

17
00:00:57.083 --> 00:01:00.290
Question tag means a short question at the end of a statement.

18
00:01:00.883 --> 00:01:03.045
A question tag checks information.

19
00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.511
Your turn. Say: Question tag.

20
00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.565
Question tag.

21
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:12.202
Agreement.

22
00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:16.006
Agreement means when people have the same opinion.

23
00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:18.047
We reached an agreement.

24
00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:21.453
Your turn. Say: Agreement.

25
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.382
Agreement.

26
00:01:26.117 --> 00:01:27.269
Confirmation.

27
00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:31.200
Confirmation means a statement that something is true.

28
00:01:31.817 --> 00:01:33.363
I need confirmation.

29
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.637
Your turn. Say: Confirmation.

30
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.768
Confirmation.

31
00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:42.425
Positive.

32
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:45.172
Positive means saying yes.

33
00:01:45.783 --> 00:01:47.469
The statement is positive.

34
00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:50.469
Your turn. Say: Positive.

35
00:01:53.333 --> 00:01:54.207
Positive.

36
00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:55.858
Negative.

37
00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.548
Negative means saying no.

38
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:00.569
The tag is negative.

39
00:02:01.183 --> 00:02:03.580
Your turn. Say: Negative.

40
00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:07.318
Negative.

41
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:08.875
Checking.

42
00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:12.684
Checking means making sure something is correct.

43
00:02:13.283 --> 00:02:14.714
I am checking the time.

44
00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:17.679
Your turn. Say: Checking.

45
00:02:20.533 --> 00:02:21.407
Checking.

46
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.048
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:31.173
Visal, it is a hot day. How can you check that your friend agrees?

48
00:02:32.283 --> 00:02:41.951
It is hot, isn't it? A question tag is a short question at the end of a sentence. We use it to check information or to invite agreement.

49
00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.109
How do we make it?

50
00:02:45.217 --> 00:02:59.145
If the sentence is positive, the tag is negative: You like tea, don't you? If the sentence is negative, the tag is positive: She doesn't swim, does she? The tag repeats the helping verb.

51
00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.191
What helping verb do we use?

52
00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:16.483
The same one as in the sentence: She is tired, isn't she? They can swim, can't they? If there is no helping verb, use do, does or did. Rising voice means a real question.

53
00:03:17.633 --> 00:03:19.110
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:24.794
Grammar focus: Question tags: positive plus negative tag.

55
00:03:25.094 --> 00:03:26.455
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.662
It is hot, isn't it?

57
00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.062
You like tea, don't you?

58
00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.706
She doesn't swim, does she?

59
00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:42.822
Positive statement + negative tag; negative statement + positive tag. Use the same helping verb, then the pronoun.

60
00:03:43.583 --> 00:03:46.979
Be careful! Don't say: You like tea, aren't you?

61
00:03:48.933 --> 00:03:50.991
Say: You like tea, don't you?

62
00:03:51.291 --> 00:03:53.151
Use the same helping verb.

63
00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:56.596
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.529
Checking Together.

65
00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:00.770
It is a beautiful day, isn't it?

66
00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.441
You study English, don't you?

67
00:04:04.433 --> 00:04:06.317
She can't swim, can she?

68
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:08.706
They are coming, aren't they?

69
00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.685
A question tag is a way of checking and keeping the conversation friendly.

70
00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.779
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:19.617 --> 00:04:21.245
She is tired, blank she?

72
00:04:21.545 --> 00:04:24.699
A, is. B, isn't. C, doesn't.

73
00:04:28.233 --> 00:04:30.256
The answer is B: isn't.

74
00:04:31.417 --> 00:04:33.068
You like football, blank you?

75
00:04:33.368 --> 00:04:36.441
A, do. B, don't. C, aren't.

76
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.767
The answer is B: don't.

77
00:04:42.917 --> 00:04:44.742
He doesn't play, blank he?

78
00:04:45.042 --> 00:04:48.161
A, does. B, doesn't. C, is.

79
00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.630
The answer is A: does.

80
00:04:54.783 --> 00:04:56.655
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:56.955 --> 00:05:02.385
A, They are late, aren't they?. B, They are late, are they not?. C, They are late, don't they?.

82
00:05:05.933 --> 00:05:08.502
The answer is A: They are late, aren't they?.

83
00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:13.217
According to the reading, what keeps the conversation friendly?

84
00:05:13.517 --> 00:05:19.156
A, a question tag. B, a loud voice. C, a long story.

85
00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.675
The answer is A: a question tag.

86
00:05:26.867 --> 00:05:30.250
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:31.117 --> 00:05:34.730
Write a sentence with a question tag to check something with a friend.

88
00:05:43.517 --> 00:05:45.203
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:45.503 --> 00:05:57.622
You are my classmate, aren't you? I use a question tag to check that something is true. The statement is positive, so the tag is negative. It makes the conversation friendly.

90
00:05:57.922 --> 00:05:59.597
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:00.483 --> 00:06:06.781
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and question tags: positive plus negative tag.

92
00:06:07.081 --> 00:06:11.312
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

93
00:06:11.612 --> 00:06:14.056
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:14.356 --> 00:06:17.368
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

